<title>UK: Castrol India '96 optg profit up.</title>
<headline>Castrol India '96 optg profit up.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p> Dividend (rupee)	 5.5		    vs n/a</p>
<p> Total dividend (rupee) 8.5		    vs n/a</p>
<p> Operating profit	 1,473		  vs 1,250</p>
<p> Turnover		   8,882		  vs 7,142</p>
<p>NOTE - Britain's Burmah-Castrol Plc owns 51 percent of Bombay Stock Exchange-listed lubricants and fuels company Castrol India Ltd. The parent company said Castrol India's market share had rise to nearly 20 percent, up from about 6.0 percent in 1992. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
